{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/835569-potent-kith","id":835569,"title":"Potent Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-22T21:05:27-08:00","id":835569,"title":"Potent Kith","content":"So, there are some Kiths (like Antiquarian or Witchtooth) which don't have Wyrd as a factor anywhere in their calculations. Do these Kiths just get no benefit from the Potent Kith Merit, or is there any sort of benefit they could receive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T08:00:41-08:00","id":835780,"title":"","content":"Just go with no benefit. Its not like someone is forcing you to take the merit if you don't have an appropriate kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T08:14:49-08:00","id":835790,"title":"","content":"I like how Potent Kith dovetails nicely with Dual Kith Merit. <br /> <br /> Example a Dual Kith Dearheart Larenist that has Potent Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and a wyrd of \u2022, can drop someones composure by 3, and by spending a point of Glamour boost they're subtlefudge skill dice pool by 6, making them wicked liers. At 10 wyrd they can get dice pools of +15 on subltefudge rolls and -8 to composure for those the Changeling touches.<br /> <br /> It also dovetails beautifully with the riddle kith contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:34:56-08:00","id":835870,"title":"","content":"Not that I object to it, but it's really weird to see changeling players min-max like this. I haven't quite seen it before.<br /> <br /> I kind of like it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:43:53-08:00","id":835873,"title":"","content":"I never found any fun way to min-max beyond the occasional abuse of the 1E pledge mechanics; it seems like the most Changeling thing in the world to find loopholes in the rules and exploit them for all they're worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:51:32-08:00","id":835876,"title":"","content":"Really? My experience has been that Changeling narratively supports crazy min maxed character concepts better than most systems. Characters typically did one thing during their durance and were expected to do it inhumanly well. Player Characters in particular often did it so well that they were able to defy beings of godlike power and escape home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T11:11:12-08:00","id":835886,"title":"","content":"Yeah, got to agree with HelmsDerp. Usually changeling characters in my games are more &quot;archetypes&quot; than &quot;randy randoms.&quot; Players tend to make the Durance this all-consuming thing, so at the start of the game, changelings tend to be hyperspecialised, often defined by their Kith, Seeming and, to a lesser degree, Court. It's only once play develops that they start branching out and filling out their mechanics, rounding out the character in more natural ways.<br /> <br /> I find it mirrors the psychological consequences of trauma fairly well. At first, the trauma consumes you, and you feel defined by it. Only after you learn to move on past it, you start fleshing out as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T14:01:51-08:00","id":836013,"title":"","content":"Super specializing is even stronger and easier in Changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> An Orger Dual Kith Hunterheart/Soldier with Contract of the Wooden Fang, Terrible Brute, and Cloak of the Elements, all 10 merits dots in fighting styles is going to be awesome at fighting right out the door, like crazy rambo action.<br /> <br /> A Fairest Dearheart/Illes of the Ivory Court (or probably Spring Court), with the Luna's Bedlam Contract (which a Fairest can use to give a Target conditions like swooning, wanton, obsession, madness...) will be a Master seducer.<br /> <br /> A Fireheart/Author will be able to write a large brilliant book in less then an hour.<br /> <br /> A Wingwing/Lurkglider with can fly then fall on an enemy like a bird of prey.<br /> <br /> A Sandharrow/flamesiren Fairest can sing a song and then grapple the person they made swoon and how them till they're burnt to a crisps by your molten hot sand.<br /> <br /> A Darkling Dearheart Larcenist with Potent Kith and the Pushier feat, is a master blackmailer, Lier, and Thief (Dearheart's ability to drop composure means perception drops too, making it easier to pick pocket someone and Larcenists get an exceptional success on the roll) and as such can easily betray people and get clarity as a result. Or worse take the Terrible Harvest Contract and with a touch reap people, including Changelings, with ease. Add the Fairest Effect later on Terrible Harvest and cause your targets to swoon instead so mortals won't know what you did to them. Darkling is best for this because its possibly to use terrible harvest to betray the trust of someone or a group in such a way that you do it for the greater good which regains you a point of Clarity which pays the Clarity cost of the contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T15:40:51-08:00","id":836063,"title":"","content":"I went for the ogre gristlegrinder/render dual kith with potent kith myself. Though that begs the question... it's a potent kith. But which one? Or does it apply to both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T16:39:59-08:00","id":836095,"title":"","content":"Both, if you had to purchase it seperately for each Kith blessing, it would say so. This way it synergizes with Dual Kith and The Riddle Kith contract, which is awesome. If you have riddle kith contract, Dual Kith merit, and the potent kith merit at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you have a very flexible character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T00:04:21-08:00","id":836889,"title":"","content":"So with render+gargantuan, you can falcon punch people with a 3 damage starting weapon that only gets stronger as you bump wyrd. Or combine with earthbones+metal+cloak of the elements+mundane armor for.immunity to small-arms fire. Or Maker+cyclops to become macgyver. Or venombite+waterborn to grapple werewolves to death. Or flowering+nixie to win all persuasion rolls ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":11326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","user":"Misterscruffles","date":". 02-25-2016, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T08:10:08-08:00","id":837031,"title":"","content":"Not all perception rolls, a Wyrd 10 Broadback/Polychromatic Changeling might be able to resist you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T14:54:57-08:00","id":837229,"title":"","content":"Werewolf in Basu-Im might stand a chance too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:41:42-08:00","id":837745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/835569-potent-kith#post835569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there are some Kiths (like Antiquarian or Witchtooth) which don't have Wyrd as a factor anywhere in their calculations. Do these Kiths just get no benefit from the Potent Kith Merit, or is there any sort of benefit they could receive?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that the effects of the Merit would probably need to be determined by the Storyteller, and I do think that every kith should be able to benefit from it. I think that the way I'd handle it for most kiths would be to allow their dots in Potent Kith to be added to an appropriate Skill or Skill specialty, such as a Witchtooth getting a benefit on Occult or curses. I could also see adding Potent Kith to other traits instead, like giving a Metalflesh with it additional Health or improving the enhanced armor rating when spending Glamour to reflect their greater durability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:43:00-08:00","id":837746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/835569-potent-kith?p=837745#post837745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the effects of the Merit would probably need to be determined by the Storyteller, and I do think that every kith should be able to benefit from it. I think that the way I'd handle it for most kiths would be to allow their dots in Potent Kith to be added to an appropriate Skill or Skill specialty, such as a Witchtooth getting a benefit on Occult or curses. I could also see adding Potent Kith to other traits instead, like giving a Metalflesh with it additional Health or improving the enhanced armor rating when spending Glamour to reflect their greater durability.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'll be handling it in my games, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}